# ── SpreadWorks build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# spreadworks/frontend/dist is a TRACKED deploy artifact: the live Render
# service's build command is pip-only (it drifted from the blueprint, which
# does build the frontend), so whatever is committed here IS what ships.
#
# Marked -text -merge -diff for three reasons, each one a bug we have hit:
#   -text   core.autocrlf=true was rewriting LF->CRLF on checkout, so a
#           freshly-built dist showed as "modified" with byte-identical
#           content. That phantom churn hides a genuinely stale bundle and
#           makes any byte-level freshness check unusable.
#   -merge  git must never line-merge two minified bundles. A hand-merged
#           chunk is worse than either side; the only correct resolution is
#           to rebuild.
#   -diff   nobody reviews a minified diff, and it buries the real changes
#           in a PR.
